WEBVTT

00:00:06.584 --> 00:00:08.253
The kid, the kid!

00:00:08.253 --> 00:00:11.547
When this truck stops, I'm gonna get him.

00:00:11.547 --> 00:00:15.135
You nincompoop, don't you know where this truck always parks?

00:00:15.135 --> 00:00:17.929
Yeah. The market. At the entrance.

00:00:17.929 --> 00:00:20.473
Right next to the... Oh.

00:00:20.473 --> 00:00:22.767
[♪♪♪]

00:00:27.189 --> 00:00:28.648
[BOTH GRUNTING]

00:00:31.818 --> 00:00:34.529
This reminds me of the first time I was put in a cage.

00:00:34.529 --> 00:00:36.531
The circus was in town, and I'd always--

00:00:36.531 --> 00:00:38.074
Whiskers, stay focused.

00:00:38.074 --> 00:00:41.870
On what? Being captured and getting our comeuppance?

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:43.872
Anyway, they only hired bats,

00:00:43.872 --> 00:00:45.915
so I made a costume out of gym socks.

00:00:46.833 --> 00:00:48.543
THOMAS: Ah, there we are.

00:00:48.543 --> 00:00:51.254
[VAMPIRE WEEKEND'S "HARMONY HALL" PLAYING]

00:00:56.467 --> 00:00:58.803
♪ We took a vow in summertime ♪

00:00:58.803 --> 00:01:02.265
♪ Now we find ourselves In late December... ♪

00:01:02.265 --> 00:01:04.767
You were right. I should have just supported you.

00:01:04.767 --> 00:01:07.854
I think I was just worried the book would take you away

00:01:07.854 --> 00:01:10.940
from the family I wanted us to have, you know?

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:12.734
I'm sorry. No, I'm sorry.

00:01:12.734 --> 00:01:15.611
I was chasing something for all the wrong reasons.

00:01:15.611 --> 00:01:18.114
I lost sight of what was important.

00:01:18.114 --> 00:01:21.409
Our family. Mm. And families, I've learned,

00:01:21.409 --> 00:01:23.328
can come in all shapes and sizes.

00:01:23.328 --> 00:01:25.372
Ha! Nigel wanted me to use

00:01:25.372 --> 00:01:28.541
those exact words to end my book.

00:01:28.541 --> 00:01:31.127
You're kidding. Ha-ha-ha-ha!

00:01:31.127 --> 00:01:35.673
I mean, the sentiment's nice, but how pathetic.

00:01:35.673 --> 00:01:37.508
Right? Right? Pathetic? Yeah.

00:01:37.508 --> 00:01:39.802
That's why I said it, to make you laugh.

00:01:39.802 --> 00:01:41.596
Nigel, he was pathetic.

00:01:41.596 --> 00:01:43.181
You want some tea? BEA: Lovely.

00:01:43.181 --> 00:01:44.807
Benjamin, is now the time

00:01:44.807 --> 00:01:47.810
for my often interrupted yet heartfelt apology?

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:50.646
Mm... I'm sorry.

00:01:50.646 --> 00:01:52.899
I never should have mixed you up in all this.

00:01:52.899 --> 00:01:55.902
I got caught up worrying about who everyone thought I was,

00:01:55.902 --> 00:01:59.989
instead of who I really am, which is your brother.

00:01:59.989 --> 00:02:02.867
And your cousin, who continues to not listen to you

00:02:02.867 --> 00:02:06.413
but promises to really, really try.

00:02:06.413 --> 00:02:09.249
I'm sorry. What...?

00:02:09.249 --> 00:02:12.294
Hm. I'm kidding.

00:02:12.294 --> 00:02:15.755
But, really, Peter, from now on, you need to think things through

00:02:15.755 --> 00:02:19.675
and take some advice from those who love you.

00:02:19.675 --> 00:02:24.013
I'm sorry. Wha...?

00:02:24.013 --> 00:02:26.849
[PETER CONTINUES SUSTAINING HIGH-PITCHED TONE]

00:02:34.774 --> 00:02:36.818
Sunset.

00:02:36.818 --> 00:02:38.403
[SUPERGRASS' "ALRIGHT" PLAYING]

00:02:38.403 --> 00:02:41.614
♪ We are young, we run green ♪

00:02:41.614 --> 00:02:44.659
♪ Keep our teeth Nice and clean ♪

00:02:44.659 --> 00:02:47.662
♪ See our friends See the sights ♪

00:02:47.662 --> 00:02:49.747
♪ And feel all right... ♪

00:02:49.747 --> 00:02:52.708
NARRATOR: And so they all lived happily ever after,

00:02:52.708 --> 00:02:54.043
[BABY CRYING]

00:02:54.043 --> 00:02:55.878
as is the law in these storybooks.

00:02:55.878 --> 00:02:59.466
You just take this out, and...

00:02:59.466 --> 00:03:01.468
[BABY COOING] [BEA CHUCKLES]

00:03:01.468 --> 00:03:03.428
There.

00:03:03.428 --> 00:03:05.638
Bea and McGregor had a child of their own.

00:03:05.638 --> 00:03:08.891
And the rabbits took to her like a real sister.

00:03:08.891 --> 00:03:10.143
[SIGHS]

00:03:10.143 --> 00:03:11.978
Peekaboo.

00:03:11.978 --> 00:03:13.729
Peekaboo. Peekaboo.

00:03:13.729 --> 00:03:15.315
Peekaboo!

00:03:15.315 --> 00:03:17.484
Try this jelly bean. It'll change your life.

00:03:17.484 --> 00:03:20.236
Cotton-Tail, no. Cute baby.

00:03:20.236 --> 00:03:22.405
Right, well, if anybody needs me,

00:03:22.405 --> 00:03:24.907
I'm gonna swim to France and back.

00:03:24.907 --> 00:03:26.326
[WATER SPLASHES]

00:03:26.326 --> 00:03:29.454
I finally realized what made me different.

00:03:29.454 --> 00:03:31.498
I'm the narrator of these stories.

00:03:31.498 --> 00:03:34.292
Another classic, Flopsy. What are you gonna name it?

00:03:34.292 --> 00:03:35.710
She already did.

00:03:38.796 --> 00:03:41.424
I like it. Implies there might be more.

00:03:41.424 --> 00:03:44.844
Or this could be it. We didn't think we'd get this far.

00:03:44.844 --> 00:03:47.389
♪ We are young, we run green ♪

00:03:47.389 --> 00:03:50.599
♪ Keep our teeth Nice and clean ♪

00:03:50.599 --> 00:03:52.101
